        "## Design closed: 20261008-api-key-authentication-for-endpoints\n\nEvery endpoint except `GET /health` now requires an `x-api-key` header. The header is compared in constant time with `auth.apiKey`, which the `API_KEY` environment variable overrides. A missing, empty or wrong key gets a 401.\nPhases: 1 · decisions: 4 (0 amended) · commits be2f940..6a6eee7 · review: APPROVED\nQuestions: OQ-001 is still open. With no key configured, the server starts and refuses every request except `GET /health`; it could refuse to start instead.\n\nThe reviewer also raised two small issues that did not block approval:\n- **Line endings:** `src/main.ts` changed from Windows (CRLF) to Unix (LF) line endings, so its diff shows all 8 lines rewritten when only one changed.\n- **Config test gap:** `test/config.test.ts` reads the real `data/config.json`, so no test checks that a key set in the config file is actually read."
